From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] qmgr: BITS job properties kept and honoured; errors retried; notifications

Updaters and installers drive downloads through BITS; most of a job's
properties were stubs and its error handling was missing:

- GetTimes (creation, modification, completion), GetOwner (the creator's
  SID, through the caller's token), TakeOwnership, the owner's integrity
  level and elevation, SetDisplayName.
- Priority (kept and used: the transfer thread takes the highest-priority
  queued job, the oldest among equals), minimum retry delay, no-progress
  timeout, maximum download time (default 90 days), error count.
- Proxy settings, checked as BITS checks them and used for the transfer
  (no proxy, the named proxies with their bypass list, auto-detection, or
  the machine's).
- The notify command line (program and its command line) kept and run
  when the job is transferred or fails for good and no callback interface
  takes the notification.
- Errors: a refused or failed connection, a timeout, an unresolved name
  and HTTP 503/504 are transient: the job waits the retry delay and is
  queued again, until it has gone the no-progress timeout (or past the
  maximum download time) without progress, then it is in error. A job in
  error tells its callback (JobError, never called before) or runs the
  notify command line. Each error is counted.
- Suspend stops a transfer under way and keeps the job; a finished job is
  BG_E_INVALID_STATE.
- Added files are checked: http(s), file and local or UNC paths, full
  local names (BG_E_PROTOCOL_NOT_AVAILABLE, E_INVALIDARG).
- ReplaceRemotePrefix, file ACL flags and peer caching flags (kept; there
  are no peers here), EnumJobs lists the caller's own jobs unless
  BG_JOB_ENUM_ALL_USERS.

Wine's qmgr tests: no failures, as before.

Gate: test/bitsjob-gate.sh (64- and 32-bit; a local copy with its notify
command line, a refused connection retried then failed with the error
command line). Mutants SG_MUTANT_NO_SUSPEND, SG_MUTANT_NO_BITS_RETRY
(qmgr/job.c). The priority order is not gated (a race to stage).
